From 6fa59512c5da12fccdcca67c2a1d81d926c50b3b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andre Watson <dre@ligandal.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 22:24:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 15/32] feat(moe): dynamic expert count (fixed-k / cumprob /
 learned) fused into the Triton router, off by default

Dropped slots become id -1 with weight 0; kept slots keep their top-K weight
(k2=K normalisation). flashinfer cutlass_fused_moe skips -1 slots (GATE 1,
bitwise vs narrow reference, time tracks the expert union). Selected via
SGLANG_QWENOPT_DYNK / SGLANG_QWENOPT_DYNK_FILE; separate target/draft arms;
per-slot tau is a device tensor (graph-safe live knob). EPLB and packed topk
are refused; duplicate expert ids asserted absent (SGLANG_QWENOPT_DYNK_CHECK).
---
